--]--><!--[--><!--]--></nav></aside><div class="VPContent has-sidebar" id="VPContent" data-v-8a91d7b9 data-v-11fb087c><div class="VPDoc has-sidebar has-aside" data-v-11fb087c data-v-81950f95><!--[--><!--]--><div class="container" data-v-81950f95><div class="aside" data-v-81950f95><div class="aside-curtain" data-v-81950f95></div><div class="aside-container" data-v-81950f95><div class="aside-content" data-v-81950f95><div class="VPDocAside" data-v-81950f95 data-v-451f18c2><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--><nav aria-labelledby="doc-outline-aria-label" class="VPDocAsideOutline" data-v-451f18c2 data-v-b608682c><div class="content" data-v-b608682c><div class="outline-marker" data-v-b608682c></div><div aria-level="2" class="outline-title" id="doc-outline-aria-label" role="heading" data-v-b608682c>On this page</div><ul class="VPDocOutlineItem root" data-v-b608682c data-v-2e9af499><!--[--><!--]--></ul></div></nav><!--[--><!--]--><div class="spacer" data-v-451f18c2></div><!--[--><!--]--><!----><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class="content" data-v-81950f95><div class="content-container" data-v-81950f95><!--[--><!--]--><main class="main" data-v-81950f95><div style="position:relative;" class="vp-doc _" data-v-81950f95><div><h1 id="duratom" tabindex="-1">duratom <a class="header-anchor" href="#duratom" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;duratom&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Durable, live Jotai atoms over a Y.Doc: read typed values, write validated patches, and re-render only when what an atom shows changes.</p><p>A <a href="https://docs.yjs.dev" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Y.Doc</a> is the shared, conflict-free state that sync providers keep the same on every device. duratom turns a node of it into a Jotai atom: you read a value your schema has checked, you write a patch that is merged into the doc and validated first, and a component re-renders only when the value it shows changes, whoever changed the doc. Persistence and network sync come from existing Yjs providers; duratom has no provider code of its own.</p><h2 id="install" tabindex="-1">Install <a class="header-anchor" href="#install" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Install&quot;">​</a></h2><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">npm</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> install</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> duratom</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> jotai</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> jotai-family</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> yjs</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Add a <a href="https://standardschema.dev" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Standard Schema</a> validator for typed atoms, such as zod, valibot or arktype, and React for <code>duratom/react</code>. duratom needs <code>yjs</code> 13.6.33 or later, <code>jotai</code> 2.9 or later and <code>jotai-family</code>.</p><h2 id="quick-start" tabindex="-1">Quick start <a class="header-anchor" href="#quick-start" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Quick start&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Paste this into <code>src/main.tsx</code> of a new Vite React app (<code>npm create vite@latest my-app -- --template react-ts</code>), then <code>npm install duratom jotai jotai-family yjs zod</code> and <code>npm run dev</code>.</p><div class="language-tsx vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">tsx</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D;">// src/main.tsx of a new Vite React app: npm create vite@latest my-app -- --template react-ts</span></span>
